# Reviewed trivy config-scan findings, accepted rather than fixed.
# Full reasoning in docs/owasp-security-review.md. Do not add an entry here
# without a review note in that document -- this file suppresses real scan
# output, so every line needs a reason someone else can check.

# KSV-01010: flags k8s/configmap.yaml's POSTGRES_PORT key as "sensitive
# content" on a generic keyword heuristic. The value is the literal port
# number 5432, not a credential -- POSTGRES_USER/POSTGRES_PASSWORD already
# live in k8s/secret.example.yaml (a real Secret object), not this ConfigMap.
# See docs/owasp-security-review.md "API2:2023 - Broken Authentication" /
# secrets handling section.
AVD-KSV-01010

# KSV-0113: flags k8s/rbac.yaml's inventory-api-config-reader Role for having
# any get/watch access to the "secrets" resource type, regardless of scope.
# This Role is restricted via resourceNames to exactly one named Secret
# (inventory-db-credentials) in one namespace -- the resourceNames scoping
# IS the mitigation this rule exists to encourage, not a gap. See
# docs/threat-model.md "Existing Security Controls" and
# docs/owasp-security-review.md "API5:2023 - Broken Function Level
# Authorization".
AVD-KSV-0113
